---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import WaveformLab from "../../components/WaveformLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Diversification: Waveforms"
  description="Diversification from first principles: how out-of-phase ups and downs cancel out, shown as interfering waves."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool · Part 1</p>
    <h1>Diversification, as waves</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Before the noise of real markets, here's the pure idea. Picture each
      asset's ups and downs as a smooth wave. When two assets don't move in
      lockstep, their waves are <em>out of phase</em> — and where one is up, the
      other is often down. Add them together and the bumps partly cancel. That
      cancellation is diversification.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <WaveformLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What you're looking at</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Top band:</strong> each asset as a wave. Taller wave = more
          volatile (bigger swings). Its <strong>correlation</strong> sets its
          phase: at +1 the waves line up; at −1 they're mirror images.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bottom band:</strong> your weighted portfolio — the sum of the
          waves. The dashed lines mark how big the swing <em>would</em> be if the
          waves simply stacked. The gap down to the solid wave is the risk that
          cancelled away.
        </li>
        <li>
          Slide the correlation toward <strong>−1</strong> and watch the
          portfolio wave flatten toward a straight line — near-perfect
          cancellation, the "free lunch" in its purest form.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is deliberately idealized: real returns don't repeat in tidy sine
        waves, and they never cancel this perfectly. Next, add real randomness in
        <a href="/tools/randomness">Part 2: Randomness</a> — then see it all
        together in the
        <a href="/tools/portfolio">Portfolio Diversification Lab</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextTool current="/tools/waveforms" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
